WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.870
In 2006, researchers in Hunan,

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:07.040
China, gave poor families
vouchers that made rice cheaper.

3
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.660
Every demand curve you have
drawn says they should buy more.

4
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.680
Many of them bought less.

5
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:17.810
The researchers called it the first
real-world evidence of upward-sloping demand.

6
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:19.370
So when rice got cheaper,

7
00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.150
why did some very poor
families buy less of it?

8
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:26.600
In this mission, you'll draw budget
lines and indifference curves,

9
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.400
and find the best choice
a family can afford.

10
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.020
Then you'll split one price
change into two separate effects,

11
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.940
and test them in the graph lab.

12
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.620
Your mission: find out how a price cut can

13
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.710
leave people eating less of a food.
